## The red this change carries and does not cause

`driver#anOwnedFunctionIsInItsOwnersFile` is red on the base commit `ae2373cb` **itself**, run in a detached worktree of that commit (`git worktree add --detach /tmp/base-1085 ae2373cb`, removed afterwards), with exactly the two rows this tree reports:

$ cd /tmp/base-1085 && bash tools/loop/tests/loop-selftest.sh --case 'driver#anOwnedFunctionIsInItsOwnersFile'
driver#anOwnedFunctionIsInItsOwnersFile|   every function is defined in the file whose row owns it, and only there: expected '', got 'layout.tsv: report.sh defines action_add and its row does not own it
driver#anOwnedFunctionIsInItsOwnersFile| layout.tsv: state.sh defines cmd_publish_refused and its row does not own it'
--- driver#anOwnedFunctionIsInItsOwnersFile[0] (exit 1)
  every function is defined in the file whose row owns it, and only there: expected '', got 'layout.tsv: report.sh defines action_add and its row does not own it
layout.tsv: state.sh defines cmd_publish_refused and its row does not own it'
FAIL driver#anOwnedFunctionIsInItsOwnersFile
loop-selftest: 1 of 1 cases failed

This change does not add a row to it. It touches `tools/loop/layout.tsv`, and the function it adds there is in its owner's row — the case would report `evidence.sh defines blocking_findings and its row does not own it` if it were not:

$ git show ae2373cb:tools/loop/layout.tsv | grep -n "action_add\|cmd_publish_refused"
exit=1

$ git diff --name-only 4d1dea06^ 4d1dea06 -- tools/loop/report.sh tools/loop/state.sh
exit=0

$ grep -o "blocking_findings" tools/loop/layout.tsv
blocking_findings
exit=0
